    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1056">

                <pb facs="0912" n="796" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg796"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/14735.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Adjutant General to General Funston</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">War Department</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 29, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>American Consul Matamoros on March 27 telegraphed State Department that there had
                    been some firing from Brownsville, Texas, into Matamoros, Mexico. Secretary
                    State has requested Governor Texas to have local authorities take appropriate
                    precautionary measures to prevent repetition. He requests United States military
                    authorities <pb facs="0913" n="797" xml:id="pg797"/> in vicinity Brownsville be
                    instructed by wire to the end that further firing from Brownsville into
                    Matamoros be prevented. Take appropriate measures accordingly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McCain.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
